# Fronted: spec (v2)

> Fronted — *…so nobody has to front it.*
> Source of truth for product decisions: `docs/planning/concepts_brief.md`. The original spec is preserved in `docs/planning/SPEC.original.md` and is superseded wherever it conflicts (no Twilio, no Stripe, no single MOCK_MODE, no CSV export, no nudge emails, no receipt eval).

## 1. Stated assumption

ASUC (UC Berkeley student government) holds every student org's money. **Assumption, said out loud:** ASUC funds a Ramp-style virtual card program per org. The ASUC portal stays the university's official record and **has no API**. The portal is to ASUC what an ERP is to a company; card platforms sync to ERPs through APIs, this record has none, so **the agent is the sync**. A second assumption: ASUC requires an expense report per purchase (business purpose, attendees, itemized receipt).

The reimbursement branch (`funding_source=out_of_pocket`) needs no assumption: it works the way ASUC works today. *"Works today as reimbursements; if ASUC funds cards, nobody fronts money."*

Pitch line: *"Ramp enforces the policy you wrote down. Fronted applies the policy your treasurer actually uses, then files it where the university requires."*

## 2. Pipeline and modules

