## 3. Org knowledge model

Three citable sources, all in SQLite after a one-time import of `data/seed/*` (validated with zod). SQLite is the authority after import.

1. **Budget sheet** (`data/seed/budget.csv` → `budget_lines`, each with `source_row`, the sheet row number). Columns: allocated, per-head cap, max per purchase, required fields, allowed card categories. Cited as `sheet row N`.
2. **Written criteria** (`org_criteria`, IDs `C-01…`), each with `source` (bylaws, exec minutes, treasurer note) and `last_confirmed_at`. Some carry a numeric `param_cents` (e.g. C-03 GM food target $3.00/RSVP) that code uses to compute suggestions.
3. **Precedent** (`precedents`, IDs `P-01…`): past spending and treasurer decisions with notes, purpose tags, attendee counts.

Plus **events** (RSVP counts) and **school rules** (`school_rules`, quoted verbatim, IDs `ASUC-…`).

**Learning loop:** every treasurer approve/deny writes a new precedent row (`P-31`, …) carrying the treasurer's note; optionally ("Save as standing criterion") also a criterion row. The next Advisor call for the same line + purpose tag sees it and cites it.

Precedent query (no RAG): same budget line AND same purpose tag, newest first, last 12 rows.

## 4. Code vs Claude split — "Claude reads, code decides"

| Claude does | Code does |
| --- | --- |
| Extract fields from the officer message (`amount_text` verbatim, purpose, line, event phrase, attendees) | Verify `amount_text` appears verbatim in the message; parse it into cents; resolve the event and RSVPs; echo back |
| Read the receipt image into line items with category tags (amounts as text) | Parse amounts to cents; check line-sum math; alcohol (keyword list OR category tag); reconcile to the charge within $0.50 |
| Word advice (`support/caution/against/unavailable`) with citations | Compute every number as a `budget_stat` (`S-…`); substitute `[[S-…]]` placeholders; drop any reason with a nonexistent citation ID, no citation, unknown placeholder, or a raw `$` amount |
| Plan the portal fill: which control gets which payload field | Validate plan (no free values, no navigation, targets resolve to exactly one control), execute, enforce URL allowlist, idempotency |
| — | Every state transition, every block, all arithmetic, every ledger write |

All model outputs are validated with zod. On failure: retry once with the validation error; then the request moves to `needs_info` (extractor/receipt) or advice becomes `unavailable` ("no recommendation") or the filer uses the scripted fallback plan (planner). Never default to pass.

Two fixed words in the UI: a **Check** comes from code, can block, cites a rule. **Advice** comes from Claude, never blocks, cites sources. Shown in two visually distinct panels.

### Tiers

| Tier | Rules | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A — school (`school_rules`) | `ASUC-ALC` no alcohol; `ASUC-REQ` amount + purpose + line present; `ASUC-BAN` banned categories (gift cards, cash equivalents, donations, personal items) | reject / needs_info |
| B — org sheet (`org_hard_rules`, derived from the sheet) | `H-REM` remaining ≥ amount; `H-CAP` per-attendee cap; `H-MAX` max per purchase; `H-REQ` required fields per line | reject (with suggested fix) / needs_info |
| C — Advisor | soft criteria + precedent | advice only |

## 5. State machine

`transition(request, event) → {status, effects[]}` is pure; invalid transitions throw. Claude never emits events.

States: `draft, needs_info, rejected, awaiting_approval, denied, expired, approved, card_issued, purchased, receipt_received, receipt_flagged, filing_queued, filed, filing_failed, needs_human, closed, cancelled`.

Card path (`funding_source=program_card`):
```
draft ─RULES_FAILED→ rejected            draft ─RULES_NEEDS_INFO→ needs_info
draft ─RULES_PASSED→ awaiting_approval ─DENY→ denied
awaiting_approval ─EXPIRE→ expired (24h)
awaiting_approval ─APPROVE→ approved [commit, record_precedent, issue_card]
approved ─CARD_ISSUED→ card_issued
card_issued ─EXPIRE→ expired [terminate_card, release_commit]  (app-enforced card expiry)
card_issued ─TXN_SETTLED→ purchased [release_commit, record_settled, terminate_card (single use), ask_receipt]
purchased ─RECEIPT_OK→ receipt_received ─QUEUE_FILING→ filing_queued [queue_filing]
purchased ─RECEIPT_FLAGGED→ receipt_flagged ─RESOLVE_ACCEPT→ filing_queued | ─RESOLVE_CANCEL→ cancelled
purchased ─RECEIPT_ALCOHOL→ cancelled [mark_owed_back]   (card already terminated; charge stays unreconciled)
filing_queued ─FILED→ filed [record_filed] ─CLOSE→ closed
filing_queued ─FILING_FAILED→ filing_failed ─ESCALATE→ needs_human ─RETRY_FILING→ filing_queued
```
Reimbursement path (`funding_source=out_of_pocket`) enters at `receipt_received`:
```
receipt_received ─RECEIPT_ALCOHOL→ cancelled
receipt_received ─RULES_FAILED→ rejected | ─RULES_NEEDS_INFO→ needs_info | ─RULES_PASSED→ awaiting_approval
awaiting_approval ─APPROVE→ filing_queued [record_precedent, queue_filing]
```
The treasurer acts again only on `receipt_flagged`, `needs_human`, or an unreconciled card charge (alcohol cancel). Alcohol never drops lines: the whole request is cancelled.

## 6. Data model (SQLite, integer cents everywhere)

- `orgs`, `members` (role `officer|treasurer`, email, student_id; no phone numbers)
- `budget_lines` (`id`, `name`, `allocated_cents`, `per_head_cap_cents`, `max_per_purchase_cents`, `required_fields`, `allowed_categories`, `source_row`)
- `ledger_entries` (`kind`: `commit|release|card_settled|filed|adjust`, `amount_cents` signed only for adjust, `funding_source`, `line_id`, `request_id`, memo)
  - committed = Σcommit − Σrelease
  - spent = Σcard_settled + Σfiled(out_of_pocket) + Σadjust
  - unreconciled = Σcard_settled − Σfiled(program_card) + Σadjust(program_card)
  - remaining = allocated − spent − committed
- `school_rules`, `org_hard_rules`, `org_criteria` (`source`, `last_confirmed_at`, `param_cents`), `precedents` (outcome, treasurer note, purpose tag, attendees, semester), `events` (RSVPs)
- `requests` (`short_id` `R-12`, status, funding_source, amount_cents, approved_amount_cents, line_id, event_id, attendee_count, purpose, purpose_tag, extraction_json), `rule_results`, `recommendations` (verdict, reasons_json, dropped_json), `approvals`
- `cards` (`issuer`, `external_card_id`, `last4`, `limit_cents`, `allowed_categories`, `expires_at`, `status`), `card_transactions` (unique `external_transaction_id`)
- `receipts` (unique `sha256`, extraction_json, parsed totals, flags), `portal_filings` (`form_type`, unique `idempotency_key`, `payload_json`, `plan_json`, `confirmation_id`, `status`, attempts)
- `audit_log` (request_id, trace_id, kind, site, model, latency_ms, mode, data_json, screenshot)
- `chat_messages` (simulator transcript)
- `mock_issuer_cards`, `mock_portal_submissions` — state owned by the mock external systems.

## 7. Interfaces and switches

```ts
interface CardIssuer {
  readonly name: 'mock';
  createCard(i: CreateCardInput): Promise<IssuedCard>;
  getCard(externalCardId: string): Promise<IssuedCard>;
  terminateCard(externalCardId: string): Promise<IssuedCard>;
}
type TransactionSettledEvent = { type: 'transaction.settled'; event_id; external_card_id; external_transaction_id; amount_cents; merchant_name; merchant_category; settled_at };
```
"Simulate purchase" asks the mock issuer to authorize; on success it emits a normalized `transaction.settled` event into `handleIssuerEvent` — the same handler `POST /api/issuer/events` uses. The field names are ours, *modeled on a typical card-issuing API*; never claimed Ramp-compatible.

Claude wrapper: `callClaude({site, fixtureKey, schemaVersion, schema, system, content})`. Replay recordings live at `fixtures/replays/<site>/<fixtureKey>.v<schemaVersion>.json` — keyed by site + fixtureKey + schemaVersion, **not** a prompt hash. Missing recording in replay = hard error (and a stub with the input is written to `fixtures/replays/_missing/` for authoring). Fixture keys: extractor = normalized message slug; receipt = image sha256 prefix; advisor = request slug + hash of the knowledge rows it sees (IDs + notes); planner = hash of the snapshot structure (roles/names/errors, not values) + payload shape.

Switches (env): `CLAUDE_MODE=live|replay` (default replay), `PORTAL_RUNNER=headed|headless`, `ISSUER=mock`, `CLAUDE_MODEL_*` model overrides (default `claude-sonnet-5-5`), `CARD_BUFFER_PCT=20`, `RECEIPT_TOLERANCE_CENTS=50`, `PORTAL_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`.

Plan step (strict zod object, no extra keys):
```ts
{ action: 'fill'|'select'|'check'|'upload'|'click', target: { role, name }, value_ref?: keyof FilingPayload }
```
fill/select/upload require `value_ref`; check/click forbid it. Roles allowed: textbox, combobox, checkbox, button, file. Links and any navigation are impossible by construction. Each target must match exactly one control in the snapshot and exactly one element at execution.

Idempotency in three places: unique `portal_filings.idempotency_key` (`FRONTED-R-12`), the mock portal rejects a duplicate `external_ref` server-side, the worker skips any job that already has a `confirmation_id`.

## 8. Demo script (3 minutes, replay mode)

1. **Reject with a fix (org rule, not alcohol):** officer: "Can I spend $120 on stickers for Calapalooza tabling?" → Tier B `H-REM`: Marketing has $85.50 left (sheet row 4). Suggested fix shown.
2. **Pass but flagged from precedent:** "Can I spend $50 on pizza for Thursday's GM?" → echo-back → all checks pass → Advice *caution*: $4.17/head for 12 RSVPs vs last 5 GMs' $2.90 (P-14, P-19), C-03 suggests $36.
3. **Treasurer approves once, with a note** ("Thursday is our recruiting GM…") → note becomes P-31.
4. **Card:** last 4, limit $60.00 (+20% buffer), food categories, expiry 2 days after the event.
5. **Simulate purchase** $48.73 → normalized event → receipt photo → Claude reads it, code reconciles (within $0.50).
6. **Browser agent** files the expense report in the mock ASUC portal, hits the date-format validation error, fixes it, gets a confirmation ID. Budget panel updates.
7. **Learning loop:** "Can I spend $60 on pizza for next Thursday's recruiting GM?" → advice now *supports*, citing P-31.
8. (Optional) Reimbursement: hardware receipt already paid → same pipeline, personal-funds payee section in the portal. (Optional) Beer receipt → whole request cancelled, card terminated, $59.52 shown unreconciled.

## 9. In scope (48h)

Simulator (officer pane, treasurer pane, side panel: budget, unreconciled, live agent trace), mock ASUC portal (one form, payment method, payee only for personal funds, deliberate date-format error, duplicate rejection, confirmation ID), portal worker, mock issuer, the three tiers, the learning loop, reimbursement flag, replay recordings for every demo call, `npm run demo|reset|record|test|e2e|typecheck`.

